@startuml rendering_concept_layers
title rendering context -- layer-first, CONCEPT as the separator inside each layer\nThe SAME four concepts (render_group, job, allocation, fleet) appear in every layer -- trace any one straight down.\nOne bounded context; concepts collaborate INSIDE it. Only identity + billing are separate contexts, reached via ports.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classBackgroundColor #fafafa
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 42

package "serverV2" as SV #f7f7f7 {

  package "rendering   (render-pipeline context)" as REN #ffffff {

    package "domain" as DOM #fef3c7 {
      class "render_group\ngroup_status_policy\nterminal_cost_rollup\ninvariants" as D_RG
      class "job\njob_counts\nretry_policy\nchunk_actual_cost" as D_JOB
      class "allocation\ntiers\ncomposite_scorer\nanalyzers" as D_ALLOC
      class "fleet\nstrategy_rules\nfleet_capability" as D_FLEET
    }

    package "application" as APP #d8f5d0 {
      class "render_group\ncreate confirm_upload cancel delete\nreconcile queries" as A_RG
      class "job\nworker_start status progress outputs\nsuccess failure retry handlers" as A_JOB
      class "allocation\nplan submit estimate_cost\npending dispatch queues" as A_ALLOC
      class "fleet\ndispatch monitor_tick\ncancel_at_fleet" as A_FLEET
      class "ports\nEXTERNAL edges only\nIUserService  ICreditsService" as A_PORTS #ede9fe
    }

    package "presentation" as PRES #dbeafe {
      class "render_group\nrouters + presenters" as P_RG
      class "job\nworker-callback routers" as P_JOB
      class "allocation\nmachines + pending-queue routers" as P_ALLOC
      class "fleet\ncommunity + docker + instance routers" as P_FLEET
    }

    package "infrastructure" as INFRA #fee2e2 {
      class "render_group\nRenderGroupRepository" as I_RG
      class "job\nJob Repo · InProgress · OutputFrame · Telemetry" as I_JOB
      class "allocation\nPending/Dispatch repos · Machine · AllocationClient" as I_ALLOC
      class "fleet\nFleetRegistry · Vast/Modal/community clients" as I_FLEET
    }

    class "bootstrap.py\none build per concept, composed" as BOOT #eef2ff
  }

  package "identity   (context)" as IDN #e5e7eb {
    class "users\nprofile · auth · signup" as U_USERS
  }

  package "billing   (context)" as BIL #e5e7eb {
    class "credits\nledger · charge · grant · balance" as B_CREDITS
  }

  package "core   (shared kernel)" as CORE #e5e7eb {
    class "RenderGroup · RenderJob\nGroupStatusResult · enums" as KERNEL
  }
}

' ---- external cross-context edges (the only ports that leave rendering) ----
A_PORTS --> U_USERS : IUserService
A_PORTS --> B_CREDITS : ICreditsService

' ---- everyone depends inward on the shared kernel ----
DOM ..> CORE

note as NTRACE #eef2ff
  Concept traceability
  ==
  Every layer is split by the SAME four concepts, colour-matched by layer.
  Read a column top-to-bottom to see one concept whole:
  render_group  domain -> application -> presentation -> infrastructure.
end note

note as NRULES #fff7ed
  The rules this encodes
  ==
  * Layers depend INWARD: presentation / infrastructure -> application -> domain.
  * job / allocation / fleet are concepts INSIDE this context -- they
    collaborate directly, NOT through cross-context ports.
  * Each concept co-locates its own repository interface at the infra
    boundary; application/ports/ holds ONLY the external edges.
  * Only identity + billing are separate contexts (their own 4 layers),
    reached via IUserService / ICreditsService and, in reverse, events.
end note

@enduml
